==Overview==
The Inventory is viewed on the [[Subscreen]]—the two terms are synonymous in games where the Inventory comprises the entire Subscreen. It is divided into sections for the different types of items, namely items assigned to buttons, [[Equipment]], quest items, and collectibles. These different types of items may appear in different sections of the same screen, or on different screens entirely: the [[Items]] screen (for selected items), the [[Quest Status Screen]], the [[Equipment Subscreen]], the [[Collection Screen]], and/or the [[Gear]] screen.

==={{TLoZ|-}}===
[[File:TLoZ Inventory.png|thumb|right|300px|The Inventory screen from {{TLoZ|-}}]]
In {{TLoZ}}, the Subscreen is accessed by pressing the [[Controller Buttons|START]] button. At the top of the screen are icons showing if Link has collected the [[Raft]], the [[Book of Magic]], the [[Blue Ring|Blue]] or [[Red Ring]]s, the [[Ladder]], the [[Magical Key]], and the [[Power Bracelet]]. Below that is an item box containing, from left to right and top to bottom, the [[Boomerang]] or [[Magical Boomerang]], [[Bomb]]s, the [[Bow]] and [[Silver Arrow]]s, the [[Red Candle|Red]] or [[Blue Candle]], the [[Whistle]], the [[Food]], the [[Letter]], [[Red Potion]], or [[Blue Potion]], and the [[Magical Rod]]. The number of collected [[Triforce Shard]]s, [[Rupee]]s, [[Key]]s, Bombs, and [[Heart Container]]s can also be seen, as well as the [[Sword]] and item currently equipped to the [[Controller Buttons|B]] button.

